OL,3,ACelebrity loses injunction bid but will
OL,4,Astay anonymous pending appeal
OL,5,
OL,6,FA celebrity who asked the High Court to
OL,7,Fpermanently prevent two news
OL,8,Forganisations from publishing his
OL,9,Fidentity and allegations of sexual
OL,10,Fmisconduct has lost his case, with the
OL,11,Fcourt saying the man's claim for an
OL,12,Finjunction was denied.
OL,14,FBut the judge said a temporary
OL,15,Finjunction preventing the man from
OL,16,Fbeing named and the allegations
OL,17,Fpublished should remain in place, in
OL,18,Forder to allow the celebrity to appeal
OL,19,Fagainst the judgment, with anonymity
OL,20,Fand reporting restrictions remaining in
OL,21,Fforce during the period allowed for any
OL,22,Fappeal.
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/18
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,164,160,200,105,0,100
